   "gap": "Account for every promised proof or evidence claim in the selected source extent and fix the finite dependent-source set before authoring those claims. The theorems the source reports as shown are only named: they are not proved and not entered in a declared finite dependent-source set. These are Lewis's diachronic Dutch book for conditionalization and Skyrms's converse (p. 244), van Fraassen's Dutch book and Easwaran's expected-accuracy argument for Reflection (p. 243), the Armendt/Skyrms diachronic Dutch book for Jeffrey conditioning (p. 245), Savage's representation theorem (p. 241), and the De Bona-Staffel result that the Kullback-Leibler accuracy improvement holds for log-inaccuracy but not for the Brier score (p. 247). The source's own Kullback-Leibler repair value for (0.3,0.4), reported as (0.438,0.572) on p. 247, is neither reported nor reconciled with the handbook's (3/7,4/7).",
